            <ArticleTitle>Laser recannalization of atheromatous vessels using fiber optics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>353-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A laser endoscope was devised using optic fibers in order to provide a means of visualization and removal of atheromatous plaques from arteries in cadavers and experimental animals. Atheromatous plaques were satisfactorily lased off in a few seconds, although contraction of lased vessels was observed. A self-focusing fiber was shown to provide laser access to and visualization of the body via a single optic fiber of feasibly less than 0.2 mm diameter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
